```

There is no typecheck or lint configured in this repo — only `bun test`.

**One decision the plan did not spell out**

My first version failed my own test: with a plain "pop if non-empty", `'../a/../../b'` returned `'b'`, because the second `..` popped the earlier unresolvable `..` instead of stacking. The fix treats a trailing `..` in the output as unresolvable, so `..` never consumes it — this is what makes `'../a/../../b'` → `'../../b'` and `'a/../../b'` → `'../b'`. Two edge cases I resolved as the natural reading of the spec: `'/..'` normalizes to `'/'` (root absorbs it, trailing slash stays because it is the root) and `''` → `'.'` (nothing left).

